summary: 'Shipped GitHub out of the gate behind a thin agnostic-ready SyncProvider seam (decision TD-2026-06-13-768), per Matt''s agnostic + github-first + fully-local tenets. 2a: external_ref generalized {kind}→{provider} (healed on read), SyncProvider interface (no pull — two-way structurally absent) + registry + GitHub impl via gh (no OAuth/server) + claimant-projection (human→assignee, archetype/peer→unassigned+marker-label) + task link/push. 2b: the symbol-aware wedge — task done runs ripple (best-effort), and the post-commit Symbols: trailer → issue comment via a provider-agnostic best-effort task sync-commit delegate. Fully local-first: core never imports providers; no provider ⇒ clean no-op. Build clean; mcp 425, cli 441.'
