learnings:
  - 'The agnostic-ready-but-GitHub-only-implemented shape reconciled Matt''s ''agnostic'' ask with Jinx''s YAGNI: a 5-method interface that earns itself with GitHub alone, pull/two-way structurally ABSENT (can''t be half-built), GitLab/Jira gated. Agnostic POLICY (claimant projection, the registry) is built; agnostic IMPLEMENTATIONS are not. That''s the honest middle.'
  - Builder caught that the post-commit hook is NOT generator-managed — it's an inline template literal in hooks/index.ts, absent from generated-hooks.ts. The brief's 'edit scripts/ + regenerate' assumption was wrong; verifying the actual source (and testing the INSTALLED hook in a scratch repo) found the truth. Don't trust a hook-source assumption; check where the string actually lives.
  - external_ref {kind}→{provider} migration rippled into task-bridge tests (stale {kind:'orchestration'} assertions) — the impl produced the healed {provider} shape correctly; only the test expectations were stale. The normalizeTask heal makes the migration safe by-construction; tests just needed the new shape.
